9. Conclusion

We have presented a fully rigorous unified theory of bounded cognition in which perception, reasoning, memory, and their compositions are governed by the single imperative of maximizing Future Value. The Universal Cognitive Bellman Theorem proves that FV is necessary for any bounded‑rational agent. From the internal structure of state transitions, we derived a composition operator that automatically yields hierarchical emergence of irreducible operations, guaranteeing that an agent’s cognitive capacity can grow without bound. The theory comes with constructive algorithms and sample complexity bounds, and we have laid out a clear roadmap for the global AI community to transform these theoretical results into a functional superintelligent architecture. No experiments are needed within this paper — our contribution is the normative blueprint, the mathematical engine that humanity can now build.

