Appendix H. Roadmap Commentary

The above proofs demonstrate that the unified FV principle is mathematically necessary and that hierarchical composition, while more intricate than initially assumed, still yields unbounded cognitive complexity under mild synergy conditions. The AI community can implement the theory by building:

1. A world model that estimates V^* and U.
2. A library of primitive operations.
3. A meta‑controller that evaluates FV for sequences via the recursion (C.2) and proposes new compositions.
4. Pruning mechanisms to manage the combinatorial growth.

Full algorithmic details are provided in Section 6 of the main text. The corrected recursion guarantees that the agent can compute the value of any novel sequence without retraining, simply by rolling out the world model and using the existing FV estimators for sub‑sequences. This makes open‑ended cognitive growth computationally feasible.